      "rationale": "This guarded equation defines the chooseNumSpec result for the empty-interval case X > Y; it expands the mathematical summary and does not rewrite MPY execution.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-05e369c2e0f0a26d0d7e674102a669feb198db11697b02b0e440dae13cd6c789",
      "start_line": 10,
      "text": "  rule chooseNumSpec(X, Y) => -1\n    requires X >Int Y"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 15,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "18311e31edf98c4536c300005037838e4651a7b61c9d5624cbb197cfddea4789",
      "rationale": "This guarded equation defines the chooseNumSpec result for a nonempty interval whose upper endpoint is even; it is one branch of the total summary definition rather than an operational or additional mathematical rule.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-18311e31edf98c4536c300005037838e4651a7b61c9d5624cbb197cfddea4789",
      "start_line": 13,
      "text": "  rule chooseNumSpec(X, Y) => Y\n    requires X <=Int Y\n     andBool pyMod(Y, 2) ==Int 0"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 20,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "c368375f7e518bf5b5f01ece3f7c41709c726a6ea30af9bebc2373407ae0c2c9",
      "rationale": "This guarded equation defines the chooseNumSpec result when the upper endpoint is odd and its even predecessor remains in the interval; it is a case of the named result summary.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-c368375f7e518bf5b5f01ece3f7c41709c726a6ea30af9bebc2373407ae0c2c9",
      "start_line": 17,
      "text": "  rule chooseNumSpec(X, Y) => Y -Int 1\n    requires X <=Int Y\n     andBool pyMod(Y, 2) =/=Int 0\n     andBool Y -Int 1 >=Int X"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 25,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "958329aed53dacc63f3d6c9422ab4eea2c1be9b87f0cbe409620d2734fa18f44",
      "rationale": "This guarded equation completes chooseNumSpec for a nonempty interval with an odd upper endpoint whose predecessor lies below X; it defines the no-candidate result and adds no independent lemma.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-958329aed53dacc63f3d6c9422ab4eea2c1be9b87f0cbe409620d2734fa18f44",
      "start_line": 22,
      "text": "  rule chooseNumSpec(X, Y) => -1\n    requires X <=Int Y\n     andBool pyMod(Y, 2) =/=Int 0\n     andBool Y -Int 1 <Int X"
    }
